# I03.var03 v6 independent decision: GO_CONTRACT_DESIGN_ONLY

Reviewed exact frozen prospective contract `tmp/i03-var03-prospective-contract-design-v6-20261008.json`: 50,697 bytes, SHA-256 `17ab577282e2186040d93195500e9df7565db51922b75468ffe62cc60c7fb30d`. The independent read-only audit `tmp/i03-var03-independent-contract-design-audit-v6-20261008.py` is 7,329 bytes, SHA-256 `4aa275a3cd2299d30211fb7c7dc6cefa466f9b7ec69df44df5dbdd220ac00393`; it exited 0 and reported 17 accepted local/Git source pairs, 34 original parent raw records, 5,210 prospective report cells per arm, five ResourceTotal mean gates, and zero new native calls. Output was returned as a tool transcript, without a separately captured binary stdout file.

The v5-to-v6 JSON change is confined to `schema`, `source_lineage.draft_history`, and `native_and_provenance_gate.converter.stage_gate`; all other source, physical, report, numeric, and two-arm approval terms compare equal. V6 makes the 32-table type-sensitive roundtrip and valid checker receipt a pre-`calc` requirement. After `calc` exits with actual integer zero and produces the original `run.log`, the runner must verify the two exact warning records, form ownership, and 0/2/0 summary before launching `jsonreport`. The accepted OUT run log pins the literal diagnostic messages and their order. This resolves the frozen v5 contradiction without adding a native stage.

The design remains a prospective, falsifiable matched control/child experiment: both new inputs open P-CREW 3; only OUT transfer quantity 1 versus 2 and arm descriptions differ. The parent run is evidence, not rerun. Full source/typed-event/report, metadata, terminal, presentation, and exact binary32 gates remain required. Control must complete, seal, and pass before a separate fresh child preflight and approval. No generated model, case preflight, native run, or publication is approved by this design decision; those require their later exact-file gates.

Frozen v2, v4, and v5 reviewer NO_GO decisions, including the corrected FTMO interpretation, remain historical and are not overwritten. The v6 independent audit did not execute SIMLOX or alter source, raw, catalog, or Git state.
